    ["他给出了答案，让他们进入了“知识领域”，但进去的人，再也没有回来。"] = "He gave the answer, leading them into the \"Domain of Knowledge,\" but those who went in never returned.",
    ["伯德温·威瑟尔成为见习骑士时，得到了一枚护符。赏赐他的人说：“上一任主人戴着它从战场活着回来了，祝你也有这样的运气。”\n他携带这枚护符历经无数战役，一路晋升，创立了自己的苍鹰骑士团。他受过很多次伤，但每一次倒下都有人把他拖回来，就像他拖回过很多人一样。\n后来，伯德温将这枚护符赠予了麾下最得力的一名骑士。再后来，这枚护符又从这位骑士手中传递给了下一个见习骑士。每一位送走它的骑士都战功赫赫，每一位接过它的骑士都还年轻。\n交接时，他们往往只说一句：“活着回来。”\n对方答：“你也是。”\n于是二人翻身上马，走向不同道路，直到马蹄扬起的尘土迷蒙双眼。"] = "When Baldwin Wetherell became a squire, he received an amulet. The person who rewarded him said: \"The previous owner wore it and returned from the battlefield alive; I wish you the same luck.\" \n He carried this amulet through countless battles, advancing all the way, and founded his own Goshawk Knights. He had been injured many times, but every time he fell, someone dragged him back, just as he had dragged many people back. \n Later, Baldwin gifted this amulet to the most capable knight under his command. Later still, this amulet was passed from this knight to the next squire. Every knight who sent it away had great military achievements, and every knight who received it was still young. \n When handing it over, they usually only said one sentence: \"Come back alive.\" \n The other replied: \"You too.\" \n So the two turned onto their horses and walked on different paths, until the dust raised by the horse's hooves blurred their eyes.",
